{
  "configuration_id": "config_021",
  "reason": "Evidence: Our best result (config_002, acc=0.5353) uses multimodal + pca_n2000 + imagenet_vit_l + concat in singleprofile mode. All four completed experiments are singleprofile, so the effect of multiprofile (and its required aggregation step) is completely unexplored. This is the largest remaining uncertainty in the design space. Question: Does moving from singleprofile to multiprofile with avgpool aggregation improve performance when all other settings (pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, concat) are held at their known-best values? Why this experiment: config_021 is the minimal, clean extension of our best configuration—changing only the profile setting (and its coupled aggregation), which isolates the multiprofile/aggregation effect. If it outperforms config_002, it validates the added complexity and justifies further exploration of aggregation types (transformer) and other encoders in the multiprofile regime. If it underperforms, it tells us singleprofile is sufficient and we can focus budget on image-encoder or RNA-encoder variations within singleprofile. Either outcome substantially reduces uncertainty about a major design axis under a limited budget."
}

